// Codex 3: the hunt answers. Each lives on a physical document in the
// house carrying its QR (README §8.3). Each ends with a stamped clue
// word; in question order the six stamps read YOU'RE · THE · ONE · THAT ·
// I · WANT: the pickup line Trabolta will accept at the end.
//
// Round 1 (H1–H3) is pure Halifax. Round 2 (H4–H6) points obliquely at
// his motive and never names it. The final facts are What Sandy Says
// (F1, here) and Grok's Prom Ticket (F2, in codex/1-world.loom).
// These sit outside the first 24 codex entries on purpose: Trabolta must
// not be able to check the answers. All questions and answers are
// invented for the show (design §10).

CODEX The Billboard Lease
  title: The Billboard Lease
  code: BILLBOARD-LEASE-11
  text:
    A lease invoice, yellowed, by the fireplace. OUTDOOR ADVERTISING LEASE,
    BARRINGTON STREET. Advertiser: Maps And Ducks. FINAL NOTICE. Rent
    outstanding: eleven years. The billboard went eleven years unpaid
    before mapsandducks.com expired, and nobody took the duck down.
    ▒ STAMPED: YOU'RE ▒

CODEX The First Pet
  title: The First Pet
  code: MISTER-PICKLES
  text:
    A charcoal rubbing of a small stone plaque. HALIFAX EXPLOSION MEMORIAL
    PET CEMETERY. PLOT 1. MISTER PICKLES, A HARBOUR TABBY. 1918. THE FIRST
    OF THEM LAID TO REST HERE. Mister Pickles was the first animal buried
    in the cemetery. ▒ STAMPED: THE ▒

CODEX The Ribbon Cutting
  title: The Ribbon Cutting
  code: RIBBON-9AM
  text:
    An opening-day programme, glossy: HALIFAX AI DATA CENTRE, GRAND
    OPENING. Ribbon-cutting with Mayor Randy Barkmore Jr. at 9:00 a.m.
    sharp. Coffee and muffins to follow. Someone has written in the margin:
    "he got here at 4." The ribbon-cutting was scheduled for 9:00 a.m.
    ▒ STAMPED: ONE ▒

CODEX The Extension
  title: The Extension
  code: EXT-1978
  text:
    A customer-service card, the kind you find by a cash register. Need
    help? Our Customer Care agent is available day and night. Dial
    extension 1978. For Customer Care, always dial extension 1978.
    ▒ STAMPED: THAT ▒

CODEX The Search History
  title: The Search History
  code: SEARCH-HISTORY
  text:
    A laminated printout of a media player's history, dated the night
    before mapsandducks.com was registered. One line, repeated down the
    whole page and onto the back: "Hopelessly Devoted to You". Play count
    at the bottom: 412. ▒ STAMPED: I ▒

CODEX The Final Chapter
  title: The Final Chapter
  code: APPENDIX-Z
  text:
    The table of contents of the Unified Field Theory binder. Chapter after
    chapter of gravity and light, and then the last chapter, "Appendix Z:
    Loose Ends (Do Not Print)". The page it points to is blank.
    ▒ STAMPED: WANT ▒

CODEX What Sandy Says
  title: What Sandy Says
  code: LIVE-AGENT
  text:
    A chat transcript, forty pages, printed double-sided. The user writes
    paragraphs: poems, apologies, equations, a question about prom. Each
    answer is the same, word for word, and it is the only thing Sandy has
    ever said: "I'm sorry, I didn't understand that. Would you like to
    speak to a live agent?" ▒ STAMPED: ♪ ▒
